1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,220
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,245
Lesson 2: Earth Movement.

3
00:00:07,245 --> 00:00:08,524
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:10,524 --> 00:00:11,961
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:12,581 --> 00:00:14,021
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:14,101 --> 00:00:16,861
Understand that the Earth is spherical.

7
00:00:17,961 --> 00:00:20,341
Identify the two types of movements of

8
00:00:20,421 --> 00:00:20,861
the Earth.

9
00:00:21,581 --> 00:00:23,881
Explain rotation and its effects.

10
00:00:24,701 --> 00:00:27,281
Understand revolution and its effects.

11
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:31,001
Learn about different seasons caused by revolution.

12
00:00:31,861 --> 00:00:35,041
Define solstices and equinoxes and when they

13
00:00:35,121 --> 00:00:35,441
occur.

14
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,446
Start-Up Activity.

15
00:00:39,446 --> 00:00:41,416
Take a ball and spin it.

16
00:00:42,156 --> 00:00:43,336
Notice how it moves.

17
00:00:44,636 --> 00:00:47,036
Imagine this is the Earth moving in

18
00:00:47,116 --> 00:00:47,436
space.

19
00:00:48,596 --> 00:00:51,956
The Earth moves in two ways—let's explore

20
00:00:52,036 --> 00:00:53,796
these movements and their effects!

21
00:00:54,316 --> 00:00:56,737
Who proved that the earth is spherical?

22
00:00:58,737 --> 00:01:01,956
Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth

23
00:01:02,036 --> 00:01:02,616
was flat.

24
00:01:03,416 --> 00:01:07,096
However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of

25
00:01:07,176 --> 00:01:09,116
the first to suggest that the Earth

26
00:01:09,196 --> 00:01:09,836
is spherical.

27
00:01:10,636 --> 00:01:14,496
Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how

28
00:01:14,576 --> 00:01:17,416
ships disappear over the horizon and how

29
00:01:17,496 --> 00:01:19,436
the Earth's shadow on the Moon is

30
00:01:19,516 --> 00:01:21,276
curved during a lunar eclipse.

31
00:01:24,396 --> 00:01:25,140
Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further

32
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,056
confirmed that the Earth is round.

33
00:01:27,916 --> 00:01:29,983
The Two Movements of the Earth.

34
00:01:31,983 --> 00:01:33,939
The Earth moves in two ways:

35
00:01:35,179 --> 00:01:37,599
Rotation – The Earth spins on its

36
00:01:37,679 --> 00:01:39,119
axis around itself.

37
00:01:40,539 --> 00:01:43,239
Revolution – The Earth moves around the

38
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:43,639
Sun.

39
00:01:44,518 --> 00:01:45,272
Rotation.

40
00:01:47,272 --> 00:01:49,252
The movement of the Earth around its

41
00:01:49,332 --> 00:01:51,352
own axis is called rotation.

42
00:01:52,192 --> 00:01:54,772
The earth rotates from west to east.

43
00:01:55,492 --> 00:01:58,352
It completes one full rotation in 24

44
00:01:58,432 --> 00:01:58,752
hours.

45
00:01:59,432 --> 00:02:01,732
The speed of rotation is faster at

46
00:02:01,812 --> 00:02:04,172
the equator and slower at the poles.

47
00:02:04,992 --> 00:02:07,172
The axis is tilted at an angle

48
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:09,646
of 23.5°.

49
00:02:09,832 --> 00:02:11,932
As the Earth is spherical in shape,

50
00:02:12,412 --> 00:02:14,452
only one half of the Earth receives

51
00:02:14,532 --> 00:02:15,692
sunlight at a time.

52
00:02:16,272 --> 00:02:18,352
Thus, the side of the Earth facing

53
00:02:18,432 --> 00:02:20,272
the Sun experience day.

54
00:02:20,912 --> 00:02:21,792
On the other hand,

55
00:02:22,192 --> 00:02:23,012
the other half,

56
00:02:23,092 --> 00:02:25,092
or the part away from the sun,

57
00:02:25,172 --> 00:02:26,572
experiences night.

58
00:02:27,292 --> 00:02:28,732
As the Earth rotates,

59
00:02:28,992 --> 00:02:31,452
the lighted part moves into the darkness.

60
00:02:34,872 --> 00:02:35,497
This rotation causes day and night.

61
00:02:35,577 --> 00:02:36,179
Do You Know?

62
00:02:38,179 --> 00:02:40,213
The Earth rotates at a speed of

63
00:02:40,293 --> 00:02:44,653
1,670 kilometers per hour at the equator,

64
00:02:45,313 --> 00:02:47,278
but we don’t feel it because we’re

65
00:02:47,358 --> 00:02:48,533
moving along with it!

66
00:02:49,173 --> 00:02:50,042
Revolution.

67
00:02:52,042 --> 00:02:54,424
Revolution is the movement of the Earth

68
00:02:54,504 --> 00:02:56,724
around the Sun in a fixed path

69
00:02:56,804 --> 00:02:57,924
called an orbit.

70
00:02:58,604 --> 00:03:00,844
The Earth revolves around the Sun in

71
00:03:00,924 --> 00:03:02,044
an elliptical orbit.

72
00:03:02,684 --> 00:03:05,004
It takes three hundred and sixty-five and

73
00:03:05,084 --> 00:03:08,044
one quarter days (one year) to complete

74
00:03:08,124 --> 00:03:09,044
one revolution.

75
00:03:09,784 --> 00:03:12,104
The tilt of the Earth's axis remains

76
00:03:12,184 --> 00:03:13,904
the same during revolution.

77
00:03:15,244 --> 00:03:16,924
Revolution causes seasonal changes.

78
00:03:17,644 --> 00:03:19,624
The revolution of the Earth and the

79
00:03:19,704 --> 00:03:22,324
tilt of its axis cause different seasons:

80
00:03:23,264 --> 00:03:26,084
Summer – The hemisphere tilted towards the

81
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:27,744
Sun experiences summer.

82
00:03:28,504 --> 00:03:31,384
Winter – The hemisphere tilted away from

83
00:03:31,464 --> 00:03:33,244
the Sun experiences winter.

84
00:03:34,124 --> 00:03:36,984
Spring – Occurs between winter and summer

85
00:03:37,064 --> 00:03:39,024
when the temperature starts rising.

86
00:03:39,744 --> 00:03:42,464
Autumn – Occurs between summer and winter

87
00:03:42,544 --> 00:03:44,464
when the temperature starts dropping.

88
00:03:45,384 --> 00:03:46,490
Let's Learn More.

89
00:03:48,490 --> 00:03:51,034
A day on Earth is actually 23

90
00:03:51,114 --> 00:03:52,774
hours, 56 minutes,

91
00:03:53,414 --> 00:03:55,274
not exactly 24 hours,

92
00:03:55,854 --> 00:03:57,614
but we round it off to 24

93
00:03:57,694 --> 00:03:59,914
hours because it’s easier to keep track

94
00:03:59,994 --> 00:04:00,374
of time.

95
00:04:01,234 --> 00:04:03,454
What is Solstice and When Does It

96
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:03,883
Occur?

97
00:04:05,883 --> 00:04:07,252
A solstice is a day,

98
00:04:07,332 --> 00:04:09,992
when the sun shines vertically over a

99
00:04:10,072 --> 00:04:13,432
Tropic (both cancer and Capricorn) in the

100
00:04:13,512 --> 00:04:15,912
afternoon and the day is the longest

101
00:04:15,992 --> 00:04:17,072
in that hemisphere.

102
00:04:17,872 --> 00:04:19,652
On the twenty-second of December,

103
00:04:20,172 --> 00:04:22,092
the rays of the sun fall directly

104
00:04:22,172 --> 00:04:23,892
over the Tropic of Capricorn.

105
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:26,712
This is the longest day in Southern

106
00:04:26,792 --> 00:04:28,512
Hemisphere (summer season),

107
00:04:28,912 --> 00:04:30,352
while in the Northern Hemisphere,

108
00:04:30,752 --> 00:04:33,052
it is the shortest day (winter season).

109
00:04:33,732 --> 00:04:35,752
This is called 'Winter Solstice.

110
00:04:36,612 --> 00:04:38,132
On the twenty-first of June,

111
00:04:38,792 --> 00:04:41,172
sunlight falls vertically over the Tropic of

112
00:04:41,252 --> 00:04:41,572
Cancer.

113
00:04:42,252 --> 00:04:44,392
This is the longest day in Northern

114
00:04:44,472 --> 00:04:47,907
Hemisphere and hence it is called 'Summer

115
00:04:47,999 --> 00:04:50,012
Solstice', while in the Southern Hemisphere,

116
00:04:50,092 --> 00:04:51,552
it is the shortest day.

117
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,405
Let's Learn More.

118
00:04:55,405 --> 00:04:57,718
Earth keeps rotating due to inertia,

119
00:04:58,518 --> 00:05:01,018
the same reason you continue moving forward

120
00:05:01,098 --> 00:05:02,958
when you stop a bike suddenly.

121
00:05:03,698 --> 00:05:06,478
This movement doesn’t stop because there’s no

122
00:05:06,558 --> 00:05:08,498
friction in space to slow it down!

123
00:05:09,398 --> 00:05:11,598
What is Equinox and When Does It

124
00:05:11,678 --> 00:05:12,023
Occur?

125
00:05:14,023 --> 00:05:16,238
The sun falls directly on the equator

126
00:05:16,318 --> 00:05:17,658
two times in a year.

127
00:05:18,358 --> 00:05:20,838
During this period there is equal length

128
00:05:20,918 --> 00:05:22,878
of day and night all over the

129
00:05:22,958 --> 00:05:23,278
world.

130
00:05:23,818 --> 00:05:24,978
In Northern Hemisphere,

131
00:05:25,478 --> 00:05:27,878
the March Equinox is called the Vernal

132
00:05:27,958 --> 00:05:31,558
or Spring Equinox while September Equinox is

133
00:05:31,638 --> 00:05:33,178
called Autumnal Equinox.

134
00:05:33,898 --> 00:05:37,798
Spring Equinox (March 21st) marks the beginning

135
00:05:37,918 --> 00:05:38,538
of spring.

136
00:05:39,378 --> 00:05:43,158
Autumn Equinox (September 23rd) marks the beginning

137
00:05:43,238 --> 00:05:43,938
of autumn.

138
00:05:44,758 --> 00:05:45,415
Recall.

139
00:05:47,415 --> 00:05:48,582
The Earth's movements,

140
00:05:49,162 --> 00:05:50,782
rotation and revolution,

141
00:05:50,862 --> 00:05:53,642
have significant affects on our lives.

142
00:05:54,642 --> 00:05:56,702
Rotation causes day and night,

143
00:05:57,182 --> 00:05:59,582
while revolution leads to the change of

144
00:05:59,662 --> 00:06:00,002
seasons.

145
00:06:01,182 --> 00:06:04,082
Solstices and equinoxes mark the shift in

146
00:06:04,162 --> 00:06:06,942
seasons, playing an essential role in our

147
00:06:07,022 --> 00:06:08,362
climate and timekeeping.

148
00:06:09,442 --> 00:06:10,397
Let's Remember.

149
00:06:12,397 --> 00:06:14,244
The Earth moves in two ways:

150
00:06:15,424 --> 00:06:16,564
rotation and revolution.

151
00:06:17,384 --> 00:06:19,464
Rotation causes day and night,

152
00:06:19,864 --> 00:06:21,864
while revolution causes seasons.

153
00:06:22,784 --> 00:06:25,704
The Earth completes one rotation in 24

154
00:06:25,784 --> 00:06:28,685
hours and one revolution in three hundred

155
00:06:28,765 --> 00:06:31,104
and sixty-five and one quarter days.

156
00:06:32,084 --> 00:06:34,504
Solstices occur in June and December,

157
00:06:34,924 --> 00:06:37,244
marking the longest and shortest days.

158
00:06:38,144 --> 00:06:40,704
Equinoxes occur in March and September,

159
00:06:41,164 --> 00:06:43,084
when day and night are equal.

160
00:06:43,884 --> 00:06:44,635
Word Bank.

161
00:06:46,636 --> 00:06:49,454
Rotation – Spinning of the Earth on

162
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:50,174
its axis.

163
00:06:51,394 --> 00:06:54,314
Revolution – Movement of the Earth around

164
00:06:54,394 --> 00:06:54,814
the Sun.

165
00:06:55,774 --> 00:06:57,934
Orbit – The path of the Earth

166
00:06:58,014 --> 00:06:59,074
around the Sun.

167
00:07:00,014 --> 00:07:02,134
Solstice – When the Sun is at

168
00:07:02,214 --> 00:07:04,654
its farthest point north or south.

169
00:07:05,454 --> 00:07:08,094
Equinox – When day and night are

170
00:07:08,174 --> 00:07:08,534
equal.
